ent protocols for these patients. [Data: Entities (2369), Relationships (3475, 9748, 8447)]\n\n## Importance of computed tomography in diagnosis\n\nComputed tomography (CT) is a vital imaging technique used in the diagnosis and management of SIC and its complications. It provides detailed insights into the internal structures of patients, aiding in the assessment of conditions such as pancreatitis and mesenteric pathology. CT scans are particularly valuable in critical care settings, where they help evaluate body composition and diagnose underlying issues that may contribute to complications in SIC patients. [Data: Entities (11630), Relationships (18785, 14357, 16025)]\n\n## Nutritional support strategies for SIC patients\n\nIntensive nutritional support is a critical treatment approach for patients with SIC, aimed at maintaining nutritional status and preventing malnutrition. This support often includes parenteral nutrition, which is necessary for patients who cannot absorb nutrients adequately through their remaining intestine. The relationship between SIC and nutritional support highlights the need for comprehensive care strategies tailored to the unique challenges faced by these patients. [Data: Entities (12479), Relationships (4788, 14350)]\n\n## Complications associated with Short Bowel Syndrome\n\nPatients with SIC face various complications, including acidosis D-láctica and nephrolithiasis, which arise due to the altered absorption and metabolism of nutrients. These complications necessitate careful monitoring and management to prevent further health deterioration. Understanding the potential complications associated with SIC is crucial for healthcare providers to implement effective treatment plans. [Data: Entities (12515, 12517), Relationships (14311, 14365)]", "# Teduglutide and Short Bowel Syndrome Community\n\nThis community centers around Teduglutide, a medication under investigation for treating Short Bowel Syndrome (SIC), and the STEPS study that eva